{
  "comment": "Every generated document section, its shape, and therefore its only legal writer. See CODE-CONTRACTS.md contract 1. A section-form flag (-ds/-gs/-ss/-rs) rewrites a whole section, which is correct for `narrative` and destructive for anything else: it removes sibling `- Label:` fields or a table. The heading is recorded here so a shape claim can be checked against the document itself; deriving it by scraping the library's case statement verified only the sections that scrape happened to match, and silently skipped every destructive one. test-document-sections.sh asserts plan_mutable_sections allows only narrative sections.",
  "shapes": {
    "narrative": "numbered \u00a7 N.M paragraphs; the section forms may rewrite it wholesale",
    "fields": "- Label: value lines; only -f|--field may write it, one label per call",
    "hybrid": "a paragraph label whose body is field lines; a section rewrite silently drops fields, so treat it as fields",
    "table": "a Markdown table; only its dedicated helper may write it",
    "empty": "no body in the template; becomes narrative once written"
  },
